*  gim_span_param_pattern_wrong - SILENT WRONG ANSWER.  A local bound to SPAN
*  over a PARAMETER, then matched against the function's own return variable,
*  removes the WRONG CHARACTERS: oracle ACDEF, SCRIP CDEF -- the leading A is
*  eaten along with the B.  Distinct from gim_span_self_rebind_wrong: there is
*  no self-reference here, and there the pattern is inert rather than wrong.
*  Distilled from DIFF.sno.
        DEFINE('STRIP(S1,S2)P')                 :(STRIP_END)
STRIP   STRIP  =  S1
        P  =  SPAN(S2)
        STRIP  P  =                             :(RETURN)
STRIP_END
        OUTPUT  =  STRIP('ABCDEF', 'BDF')
END
